page('/toddler/','Toddler classes from 12 months: Kiddo School','Kiddo.school toddler classes: short, calm, parent-led lessons from 12 months onward. First words grow with everyday food and home objects, one card at a time.',crumb([['Toddler']])+heading('FROM FIRST WORDS ONWARD','The school for your busy toddler.','Toddler classes on Kiddo.school keep the same calm rhythm your baby knows — one card, one voice, one short moment — while your toddler’s world gets bigger: pointing, copying and naming everything they see.')+toddlerBody());
page('/toddler/12-18-months/','Toddler classes 12–18 months: Toddler 1','What to do with a toddler at 12 to 18 months: simple food and home vocabulary flashcards with clear naming, pausing and real-object play, in short parent-led Talk & Think sessions.',crumb([['Toddler','/toddler/'],['12–18 Months']])+heading('TODDLER 1','12–18 months: first words grow up.','The Toddler 1 class. Around this age toddlers point at everything, understand far more than they can say and love naming the things they see every day, so this lesson pairs simple foods and home objects with clear, natural words.')+stagePageBody({chips:[['Age','12–18 Months'],['Class','Toddler 1'],['Subjects','Talk, thinking, recognition']],stageLessons:[fwfhLesson],subject:'Talk &amp; Think',soon:`<div class="fc-stage lesson-soon"><div class="fc-stage-pills"><span class="fc-age">Earlier stage</span><span class="fc-class">9–12 Months</span></div><h3>Start with Explorer 2</h3><p>First actions and body parts live at <a href="/baby/9-12-months/">9–12 months · Explorer 2</a>.</p></div>`}));
page('/toddler/18-24-months/','Toddler classes 18–24 months: Toddler 2','What to teach a toddler at 18 to 24 months: simple first concepts — big and small, up and down, open and closed, full and empty, one and many, in and out — through realistic picture pairs and playful parent-led comparison games.',crumb([['Toddler','/toddler/'],['18–24 Months']])+heading('TODDLER 2','18–24 months: first concepts.','The Toddler 2 class. Around this age toddlers love spotting differences — big and little, up and down, full and empty — so this lesson pairs twelve realistic pictures into six concepts you can name clearly while your toddler looks.')+stagePageBody({chips:[['Age','18–24 Months'],['Class','Toddler 2'],['Subjects','Thinking, comparison, talk']],stageLessons:[fcLesson],subject:'Think &amp; Talk',soon:`<div class="fc-stage lesson-soon"><div class="fc-stage-pills"><span class="fc-age">Earlier stage</span><span class="fc-class">12–18 Months</span></div><h3>Start with Toddler 1</h3><p>First Words: Food &amp; Home lives at <a href="/toddler/12-18-months/">12–18 months · Toddler 1</a>.</p></div>`}));
