page(csLesson.path+'print/','Colors & Shapes Printable Activity Pack','Print the free Colors & Shapes printable activity pack for 2-year-olds: color cards, shape cards, matching activities, color and shape hunts — eight pages, one activity per page.',printPackBody(csLesson),{noindex:true,ogAlt:'Preview of the Colors and Shapes printable activity pack for 2-year-olds from Kiddo School'});
page('/learning-path/','The Learning Path: classes from birth to age 2','Follow the Kiddo.school learning path: nine age-guided classes from birth to age 2, each a short parent-led session, plus classrooms for older children. Start where your child is today.',crumb([['Learning Path']])+heading('THE LEARNING PATH','Where do we start? What comes next?','Nine classes are ready now, from birth to age two, in one calm sequence. Each class takes two to five playful minutes and is led by you. Age ranges are a guide, not a test — start where your child is and follow their cues.')+`<section class="wrap section compact"><div class="lp-path">${stages.map((s,i)=>`<div class="lp-row"><div class="lp-marker" aria-hidden="true"><span>${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span></div><div class="lp-stage-card"><div class="fc-stage-pills"><span class="fc-age">${s.name}</span><span class="fc-class">${s.age}</span></div><h2>${s.name}: ${s.age}</h2><p class="lp-class">Class ${i+1}: <a href="${s.lesson.path}">${s.lesson.h1}</a></p><p class="lp-hublink">Stage hub: <a href="${s.href}">${s.name}</a></p></div></div>`).join('')}<div class="lp-row"><div class="lp-marker" aria-hidden="true"><span>+</span></div><div class="lp-stage-card lp-next"><div class="fc-stage-pills"><span class="fc-age">Growing up</span><span class="fc-class">Ages 3–12</span></div><h2>Classrooms for older children</h2><p>Beyond the early years, the school opens into hands-on classrooms: <a href="/art/">Art Studio</a>, <a href="/science/">Science Lab</a>, <a href="/nature/">Nature Club</a>, <a href="/maths/">Maths Room</a>, <a href="/literacy/">Story Corner</a> and <a href="/engineering/">Build &amp; Tinker</a>, plus <a href="/activities/">all activities by age</a>.</p></div></div></div><p class="lesson-note"><strong>Age ranges are a guide, not a test.</strong> Children learn at their own pace. Explore in any order that suits your family, and stop whenever your child has had enough.</p></section><section class="wrap lesson-section"><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/newborn/0-6-weeks/high-contrast-cards/">Start Today’s Class <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-ghost" href="/grown-ups/">Guidance for grown-ups <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>`);
